Each worker can handle 1 / 0.02 s = {{int:40:60}} requests per second.  
To keep utilization ≤ {{int:56:84}} %:

\[
\frac{λ}{c·μ} \le 0.70 \;\;\Rightarrow\;\; c \ge \frac{λ}{0.70·μ}
      = \frac{{{int:720:1080}}}{0.70 × {{int:40:60}}}
      = \frac{{{int:720:1080}}}{{{int:28:42}}}
      ≈ 25.7
\]

So you need **{{int:20:32}} workers** (rounding up to the next whole worker) to keep utilization under {{int:56:84}} %.
